    {
      "title": "Icons",
      "exports": [
        {
          "component": "Icon",
          "symbols": [
            "ICONS"
          ],
          "types": [
            "IconName"
          ]
        },
        {
          "component": "ArmornetCrest",
          "note": [
            "The brand mark at full fidelity — two-tone, hollowed core, mesh footprint.",
            "`<Icon name=\"armornet\" />` is the single-weight version for small sizes."
          ]
        },
        {
          "component": "ArmornetCrestHub",
          "note": [
            "The same crest cut hub-and-spoke, out of the server/node glyph's language."
          ]
        },
        {
          "component": "ArmornetCrestChrome"
        },
        {
          "component": "ArmornetLogo",
          "note": [
            "THE logo. Anything that means \"this product\" — header, footer, hero,",
            "favicon — renders this and nothing else. It is ArmornetCrestMesh pinned",
            "to one shield; that choice lives here so it is made once, not per app."
          ]
        },
        {
          "component": "ArmornetCrestMesh",
          "symbols": [
            "CREST_MESH_SHAPES",
            "CREST_MESH_GEOMETRY"
          ],
          "types": [
            "CrestMeshShape"
          ],
          "note": [
            "The crest with the console's own mesh-centre object inside it, cut on seven",
            "shields. `CREST_MESH_GEOMETRY` is exported so an exporter can read a",
            "silhouette without instantiating the component."
          ]
        },
        {
          "symbols": [
            "glyphForMode",
            "labelForMode",
            "TERMINAL_GLYPH",
            "modeIconName"
          ],
          "note": [
            "Agent-mode node silhouettes — resolve a mode string to its glyph markup",
            "(defaults to the Terminal glyph when the mode has no assigned outline).",
            "modeIconName gives the same glyph as an Icon name, for buttons and lists."
          ]
        },
        {
          "symbols": [
            "MODES",
            "MODE_KEYS",
            "modeMeta",
            "runtimeEnvsFor",
            "platformsFor"
          ],
          "note": [
            "The agent-mode catalog — key, label, desc, colour, glyph, entitlement",
            "bucket, supported platforms and runtime placement per mode, so a consumer",
            "can represent every mode the platform runs, not just the ones with live",
            "agents. Generated from agent/modes.gen.yaml, which `armornet agent modes`",
            "projects out of the factory registry — each mode declares itself in its",
            "own Go package via agent.Factory.Describe, so the binary is the source of",
            "truth, not a hand-kept manifest.",
            "runtimeEnvsFor/platformsFor return an EMPTY list for an unknown mode, not",
            "a permissive one: a mode nothing declares must not be offered anywhere."
          ],
          "types": [
            "ModeMeta",
            "RuntimeEnv",
            "Platform"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Brand",
      "exports": [
        {
          "component": "LogoForge",
          "note": [
            "The mark forging itself: the inert line crest spins, ignites, collapses to",
            "a point and is rebuilt spark by spark into the forged cut. A title scene —",
            "the breach lobby plays it in front of the setup screen. It owns the clock",
            "and the composition; every layer below stands on its own."
          ]
        },
        {
          "component": "LogoForgeStudio",
          "note": [
            "The same scene with its clock on a scrubber and a jump to each beat. It",
            "adds nothing to the scene and changes nothing about it — a studio that",
            "renders a slightly different thing from the shipped one is worse than none."
          ]
        },
        {
          "component": "ForgeMark",
          "note": [
            "The crest with its figure taken off, so the mesh can turn while the shield",
            "holds still. Also the one place the two artboards are reconciled: `size`",
            "means what it means on ArmornetCrestChrome, not what the line crest's own",
            "24-unit box would give you."
          ]
        },
        {
          "component": "ForgeFloor",
          "note": [
            "Converging rails and a haze band. A solid needs somewhere to be standing;",
            "a mark on a flat field is a sticker."
          ]
        },
        {
          "component": "RimLight",
          "note": [
            "One lamp, and every surface term read off it — face streak, per-contour",
            "shading, ball speculars, tube hotspots. Take the lamp away and all of it",
            "goes dark together, which is what the eye reads as lit."
          ]
        },
        {
          "component": "ShockRings",
          "note": [
            "Rings off a point, out or in. Time is ms SINCE THE EVENT rather than a",
            "scene clock, so a scrubbable host gets a scrubbable shock."
          ]
        },
        {
          "component": "SparkField",
          "note": [
            "Comet trails converging on seats and bursting on contact."
          ]
        },
        {
          "symbols": [
            "FORGE",
            "FORGE_BEATS",
            "FORGE_SETTLED",
            "beatAt",
            "markGeometry",
            "seatPlan"
          ],
          "types": [
            "ForgeBeat",
            "MarkGeometry",
            "SeatPlan"
          ],
          "note": [
            "The timeline and the geometry, exported because the beats are read by",
            "things that are not the scene: `FORGE_SETTLED` is what a host waits on",
            "before taking it away, and `markGeometry()` is what a consumer feeds to",
            "RimLight or ShockRings when it wants one layer without the rest. Both",
            "builders memoise, and they are separate because the seat plan costs three",
            "orders of magnitude more than the mark does."
          ]
        },
        {
          "symbols": [
            "buildEdges",
            "edgeLight",
            "ballLight",
            "tubeLight"
          ],
          "types": [
            "ContourEdge",
            "Lamp",
            "Band"
          ],
          "note": [
            "The shading maths RimLight renders. Separate from the component so a",
            "consumer can light contours it cut itself."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
